    "summary": "Diagnosed and repaired the failure. Root cause: support.1.dofs had longitudinal=\"free\" for the pier 1 line, which carries plain (non-sliding) laminated elastomeric bearings. Per MR-03 (板式橡胶支座的模拟), a plain elastomeric bearing provides longitudinal restraint via its shear stiffness Kh (longitudinal=\"spring\"); only PTFE sliding bearings are longitudinally free. With every support longitudinally free, the girder had no longitudinal restraint, so the stiffness matrix was singular (OpenSees error at DOF 180) and constraint L1-2 (≥2 vertical supports and ≥1 longitudinal restraint) failed.\n\nFix: re-proposed support.1.dofs = {vertical: spring, longitudinal: spring, rotation: free} citing MR-03. Support.1.Kh = 26250 kN/m (JTG3362-8.7-Kh, Ge=1.0 MPa, a=0.30 m, b=0.35 m, te=0.032 m, count=8) was already correct and unchanged; abutments 0/2/3 remain PTFE sliding with longitudinal free.\n\ngenerate_model now succeeds. Results (3-span 20+25+20 m continuous precast small-box girder, 4 girders/span, C50, self-weight only):\n- Vertical frequencies: 5.573 / 8.426 / 10.186 Hz\n- Self-weight reactions at supports 0–3: 820.5 / 2764.1 / 2764.1 / 820.5 kN\n- Self-weight midspan moments: 2690 / 2968 / 2690 kNm; support moments: −5649 kNm\n- Lane load max positive moment: 5341.5 kNm; max negative moment: −3864.0 kNm (μ = 0.288)"
